# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# A bare `go build ./examples/text` drops an executable named after the package
# in the working directory, and three of them — text, simple_pdf and genuse —
# were committed and shipped, 19.5 MB of ELF in a 24 MB module. The examples
# write to stdout now and nothing builds here on purpose, but every command's
# name is listed, because that is how they arrived: unnoticed, in a `git add -A`.
# TestGitignoreCoversEveryCommand (internal/lint) fails when a command in this
# module has a name this list does not cover. Build elsewhere, with -o.
/text
/simple_pdf
/simple_pdf17
/simple_pdfa
/extract_images
/flavored
/html_to_pdf
/sign_verify
/pdf0
/genuse
/genicc
/gensaslprep
/rulecoverage
/corpusprobe
/corpustime

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# env file
.env

# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Test data (cloned repos)
testdata/pdf20examples/

# ISO spec PDFs (copyrighted)
spec/

# Generated example output. The examples write to stdout now — or, for the one
# that produces several documents, to a directory it is told about — so nothing
# should land here. These stay as a backstop: `git add -A` swept example output
# into a commit twice, and a rule costs nothing.
output.pdf
/flavored-*.pdf
/out.pdf

# veraPDF test corpus (downloaded via `make corpus`)
testdata/verapdf-corpus/

# testdata/fuzz is deliberately NOT ignored. Go keeps the corpus it generates
# in the build cache — 21 MB of it here — and writes only two things under
# testdata/fuzz: seeds a human added, and the input that made a target fail.
# The second is a regression test that arrives exactly when it is needed, and
# ignoring the directory meant `git add` would silently skip it.


# WTPDF / PDF/UA-2 example PDFs (downloaded via `make wtpdf`); manifest + script are committed
testdata/wtpdf/*.pdf
testdata/wtpdf/.ok


# Arlington PDF Model (Apache-2.0, pdf-association) — machine-readable ISO 32000
# object grammar; cloned via `make arlington` for the structural oracle test.
testdata/arlington-pdf-model/

# Cal Poly Graphic Communications PDF/VT-1 Test File Suite — graphically-rich
# valid PDF/VT-1 files used as the FP=0 oracle for PDF/VT validation. Not
# vendored (copyrighted test content); placed here out of band.
testdata/pdfvt/

# CCITTFaxDecode sample PDFs (downloaded via `make ccitt`) — decode oracle for
# the Group 3/4 fax decoder; manifest + script are committed, files are not.
testdata/ccitt/*.pdf
testdata/ccitt/.ok

# JBIG2 sample PDFs (downloaded via `make jbig2`) — decode oracle for the JBIG2
# decoder (pdf.js conformance suite); manifest + script are committed.
testdata/jbig2/*.pdf
testdata/jbig2/.ok

# Factur-X example invoices (oracle) — not vendored
testdata/facturx/*.pdf
testdata/facturx/.ok
testdata/facturx-official/
testdata/en16931-ubl/*.xml
testdata/en16931-ubl/.ok
# The EN 16931 / CIUS oracle data moved to github.com/mgilbir/formalis with the
# rules it checks, and that module's own Makefile fetches it now (`make
# en16931-artefacts`, `make en16931-codelists`, `make cius-oracles` there; pdf0
# has no such targets). A checkout made before the move may still hold it, so it
# stays ignored here rather than turning up as untracked files.
testdata/en16931-artefacts/
testdata/en16931-codelists/*.zip
testdata/en16931-codelists/*.xlsx
testdata/en16931-codelists/genericode/
testdata/xrechnung/
testdata/peppol/
testdata/nlcius/

# Agent worktrees created by tooling under .claude/; never part of the repo.
.claude/worktrees/

# Common Crawl robustness sweep: streamed blocks, probe binary, logs and the
# quarantined reproductions. The sweep script is committed; none of this is.
testdata/cc/run/

# A CID-keyed CFF face for the font-embedding tests, fetched by `make notocjk`.
testdata/notocjk/
